# Every file here that runs as a shell script must always check out with LF
# line endings. Git for Windows checks out text files as CRLF by default,
# and a \r in a script is invisible in an editor but changes what the script
# does: it turned a hardcoded string literal in tools/check-commit-title.sh
# into a list where every entry but the last carried a trailing \r, so only
# that last entry ever matched. Forcing LF here closes that one source of
# the bug for good; it does not touch the other source, jq itself writing
# CRLF to stdout on Windows, which is handled in the script instead.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The three git hooks under .githooks/ have no extension -- a hook's name is
# fixed by git, not chosen -- so they need naming one by one rather than by
# a pattern.
.githooks/commit-msg text eol=lf
.githooks/pre-commit text eol=lf
.githooks/pre-push text eol=lf
